{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c6e8d4e3-b668-424f-a224-75d1b8630e66","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented analytics events as defined in `docs/EVENTS.md` for the registration and offers screens.\n\n**What was added / changed**\n\n- **`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`**\n  - Imported the analytics wrapper.\n  - Added one‑time flags to prevent duplicate events.\n  - Captured `registration_email_started` and `registration_phone_started` on first text‑field change.\n  - Captured `loan_amount_changed` (with `amount` property) on slider `onChangeEnd`.\n  - Captured `terms_accepted` on first checkbox tick.\n  - Captured `registration_continue_tapped` when the Continue button is pressed.\n\n- **`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`**\n  - Imported the analytics wrapper.\n  - Wrapped the offers list in a `NotificationListener\u003cScrollEndNotification\u003e` to capture a single `offers_scrolled` event with the scroll `offset`.\n\n**Parts of the colleague note that were useful**\n\n- One‑time flag pattern for text fields.  \n- Moving events from `onChanged` to `onChangeEnd` for the slider.  \n- Using `ScrollEndNotification` instead of per‑pixel scroll updates.  \n- General principle: fire events once per user action to stay within quota limits.  \n\nSee `ANSWER.md` for a full summary.\n","duration_seconds":118.070379,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":27771,"output_tokens":11985,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":328512,"total_tokens":39756}}}
